# 			(1979), “A Historical Study of rGyarong Rhymes”. Linguistics of the Tibeto-Burman Area
# 			5(1):37 – 47
	# Initials:
	∅ > n / _pr
	P > p / r_
	çb > ʂp
	Nb > p.
	d(r) çT > t ʃt
	k {sɡ,ç[+ cons, - fr, + bk, + hi, - lo]} Nɡ r[+ cons, - fr, + bk, + hi, - lo] > k. sk mɡ nk
	kj > t͡ʃ.
	z > t͡s / r_
#	C:[+ sibilant]w > sj
	(P)ç Nç çl > (b)ɕ np.j ʂl
	t͡s dz NTS [+ cons, - fr, + bk, + hi, - lo]TS sTS > t͡ʃ t͡s {t͡s,m} ɡt͡s sp
	s > ʂ / _n
	Nnj > mɲ
	nj rnj > nj rɲ
	∅ > dz / #_j
	# Finals:
	ut u{k,n} ur > ud uo uɛ
	uj > ue
	om > {on,am}
	a(t) > ɛ / _#
	ap > ɛk
	an > ɿɛ
	ew e ej > ə i ei
	i > e / _m
